{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I appears to interact with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in sialyltransferase activity. The evidence suggests that Stecholide I acts as a modulator of a pathway that ultimately leads to the activation of this kinase. The shared involvement of multiple sialyltransferase targets, including those targeted by (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, indicates a potential mechanism where Stecholide I may influence the activity of these enzymes, thereby affecting the downstream activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The consistent presence of these targets across different paths supports a unified role for Stecholide I in this signaling cascade, though the exact nature of its interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
